WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.210
With his first appearance in the original
Texas Chain Saw Massacre, Leatherface instantly

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:08.840
earned a spot among the all-time classic horror
movie villains.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.960
His story has become somewhat muddled throughout
a series of sequels, prequels, and reboots,

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.360
but don't worry, we're here to sort it out
for you.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.880
Leatherface looks like the kind of monster
that director Tobe Hooper probably saw in

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:27.240
a nightmare, but he wasn't a product of Hooper's
imagination; he and the rest of the cannibalistic

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:33.780
Sawyer family were loosely based on a real
person: serial killer and graverobber Ed Gein,

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.680
who was also known as "The Butcher of Plainfield."

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.780
Several residents of Plainfield, Wisconsin
went missing over the years, and Gein was

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.780
found responsible for their deaths.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.840
An investigation of his home resulted in authorities
finding organs stored in jars and masks made

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:50.840
of human skin.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:57.640
In The Texas Chain Saw Massacre, Leatherface
doesn't just wear one mask, he actually switches

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.740
between a few, depending on the scene.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:01.520
Why does he change his mask?

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:07.090
According to the late Gunnar Hansen, who originally
played Leatherface, the masks were not just

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:08.280
creepy accessories.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:13.060
They were actually the only way Leatherface
could really express himself.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.120
Hansen said:

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.980
"The mask really determined his personality.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:21.080
Who he wanted to be that day determined what
mask he put on.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:26.539
So when Drayton comes home with Sally, Leatherface
is wearing the 'Old Lady Mask' and he's wearing

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:31.200
an apron and carrying a wooden spoon, he wants
to be domestic, helpful in the kitchen.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.220
At dinner he wears a different face, the 'Pretty
Woman,' which has makeup."

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:41.040
In the 40-plus years since the original film
was released, different films in the franchise

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.840
have explored slightly altered "origin stories"
for Leatherface.

00:01:45.149 --> 00:01:51.220
The 2003 remake and its 2006 prequel, The
Texas Chainsaw Massacre: The Beginning, offer

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:53.180
up an interesting explanation.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:59.139
In this version, Leatherface was born disfigured
from a skin disease, and his mother dies giving

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.300
birth to him at work.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:05.920
Her boss doesn't care about the infant's fate,
so he leaves him behind in a dumpster, expecting

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:06.860
him to die.

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:13.280
A woman named Luda May Hewitt finds him and
takes him in as her own son, naming him Thomas.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:18.200
He's ashamed of the way he looks, so he begins
wearing a leather mask to hide his face.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:23.520
This habit continues into adulthood, and eventually,
the mask practically became a part of him.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:29.200
Being adopted may have saved Thomas from dying
in that dumpster, but the Hewitts aren't exactly

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:30.580
a warm, loving family.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:35.460
Just like the Sawyer family in the original
Texas Chain Saw Massacre, they're a violent

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:39.240
group of cannibals, and Leatherface is doomed
to be one of them.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:45.380
Not every film featuring a young Leatherface
depicts him as disfigured or diseased, though.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:50.900
The 2017 film Leatherface, which specifically
explores his childhood and teenage years,

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.560
takes the story in another direction.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.060
We're introduced to Leatherface as a young
boy celebrating his birthday.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:01.219
At his birthday party, his family gives him
a chance to torture and kill a thief who tried

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:02.740
to steal one of their pigs.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:07.740
But he doesn't want any part of the violent
ritual, refusing to use the chainsaw.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:11.920
Throughout the film, his mother makes it clear
that she'll make him "one of them" at any

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:12.420
cost.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:17.420
In this version of the story, it's clear that
Leatherface knows what's expected of him,

00:03:17.439 --> 00:03:19.800
but deep down, he doesn't want to participate.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.799
"Bad people like him, they're trying to break
our family apart.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:25.460
But we're not gonna let that happen, right?"

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:30.200
Despite the creepy setting of the Sawyer household,
he looks like an otherwise normal child.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:31.820
There's no sign of a skin disease.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:36.151
In fact, there's really nothing distinct about
his physical appearance that would set him

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:37.600
apart from any other kid.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.900
He's certainly not having a normal childhood,
though.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:46.040
In the movie Leatherface, the title character
spends a lot of time away from his violent

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:46.540
family.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:51.959
Young lovers Betty and Ted come across Jedidiah
Sawyer on the side of the road, Betty worries

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:55.660
about the child's safety and follows him back
to a barn, hoping to help him.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:00.480
But the Sawyer family isn't kind to strangers
on their property, and she meets an untimely

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:00.980
end.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:06.360
Her dad, the local sheriff, arrives at the
Sawyer farm; he's shocked and saddened by

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:07.700
the scene he discovers.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:13.600
As retribution, he sends Jedidiah away to
a mental institution, despite the protests

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:14.620
of his mom Verna.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:20.520
This is where the boy who will become Leatherface
spends his teenage years, under the name Jackson.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:24.560
Leatherface's Jedidiah leaves the institution
in a breakout.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:29.600
After going on the run with a nurse and small
group of inmates, he gets shot in the face,

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.360
and his mother is the one who helps him stitch
up his wounds.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:36.980
She knows that while he's vulnerable, she
can sink her claws back into him and bring

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:38.580
him back into the Sawyer family.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:43.600
When she puts a chainsaw back in his hands,
he's ready to use it for the first time, on

00:04:43.669 --> 00:04:46.300
the sheriff who sent him away and then shot
him.

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:52.231
In the 2006 prequel, it isn't Leatherface's
mother who encourages him to give in to his

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:53.500
worst impulses.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:57.420
Charlie Hewitt, Luda Mae's son, is the real
culprit.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:02.020
When Leatherface loses his job at the slaughterhouse,
he kills his boss.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:07.240
When Sheriff Hoyt tries to arrest Leatherface,
Hewitt steps in and kills him, then disguises

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.380
himself as Hoyt.

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.940
"S---, I just killed the whole f---in' sheriff's
department!"

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:18.020
After spending time with "Hoyt," the impressionable
Thomas Hewitt completely becomes Leatherface.

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:21.160
Terrence Evans, who played Old Monty in the
film, said:

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:24.260
"I think there was a chance Thomas' life could
have been different.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:29.080
But the teasing he suffered, coupled with
a bad temper, and following Hoyt around like

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:32.910
a puppy dog, left room for Hoyt to get absolute
control."

00:05:34.099 --> 00:05:38.840
In Leatherface, the character's his first
mask was from one of his first victims: the

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:42.880
nurse who left the mental institution with
him and the other inmates, Lizzy.

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:47.500
Lizzy instantly takes a liking to the young
man, but their friendship is short-lived.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:52.020
After killing Hartman, Jedidiah chases after
Lizzy with his chainsaw.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.760
She trips when her foot gets caught in a bear
trap.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:00.000
Lizzy pleads with him for mercy, but when
she insults Leatherface's mother, all hope

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.080
is lost for her.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:06.660
He swings his chainsaw, decapitates her, and
makes his first mask from her skin.

00:06:07.819 --> 00:06:12.640
In the 2006 prequel, Leatherface's killing
spree begins when health inspectors shut down

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.300
the slaughterhouse where he works.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:19.020
That matches up with the detail in the original
Texas Chain Saw Massacre, where all the men

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:21.760
in the Sawyer family worked at the local slaughterhouse.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:24.520
When they lost their jobs, they turned to
cannibalism.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:31.430
When Sally the final survivor out of her group
of friends in the 1974 film, is tortured and

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:35.770
taunted during "dinner" with the Sawyers,
they suggest that Grandpa should be the one

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:39.160
to kill her, because he was the best worker
in the old slaughterhouse.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:42.960
He's too weak to finish the job, and she escapes.

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:48.240
Leatherface is one of those classic movie
villains who wasn't necessarily born evil,

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:52.480
but knowing his backstory doesn't make the
original Texas Chain Saw Massacre any less

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:52.980
frightening.

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:56.260
Don't give any rides to strangers if you can
help it.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:57.780
"You can have dinner with us!

00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:59.660
You like head cheese?

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.820
My brother makes it real good!"

